  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between the compound 1-Methyl-6-(1-methylethylidene)bicyclo(3.1.0)hexane and SNU-387, through a series of target interactions involving carboxylesterase 2. This compound is identified as a target of multiple molecules, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, all of which are linked to SNU-387. The presence of multiple targets and their shared interaction with SNU-387 indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the enzyme carboxylesterase 2, which may play a role in modulating the activity of these compounds. The evidence suggests that the compound may influence SNU-387 through a pathway involving enzyme-mediated interactions, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
